<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2112" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴᾱς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αντος</span>,
			ὁ, <u>Ajax</u>, masc. pr. n., borne
		by two heroes, the Greater, son of Telamon, the Less, son of
		Oiïleus, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>:—nom. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἶᾰς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					68
				</span></i>
			; voc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἶαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					184
				</span></i>
			, 
				Aeol.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
					48
				</span></i>
			 A: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴαντες</span>, of
			tragedies named after Ajax, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1455b34
			</span></i>. (<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> derives it fancifully from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰαῖ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				430
			</span></i>.)</div>
